# Verani Project Context

**Verani** is a small, focused realtime SDK for Cloudflare Actors (Durable Objects) with Socket.io-like semantics. This is a **library**, not an app.

## Architecture

- **ConnectionDO** per user — one DO owns one WebSocket
- **RoomDO** per room — coordinates membership and message fanout via RPC
- Handles **hibernation** correctly (attachments, persisted state, re-join on wake)
- Horizontally scalable; no single-threaded bottleneck

**Backend API:** `defineConnection`, `createConnectionHandler`, `createRoomHandler`
**Client API:** `VeraniClient` with `on(event, handler)` / `emit(event, payload)`

## Commands (bun only)

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Install deps | `bun install` |
| Dev server | `bun run dev` (localhost:8787) |
| Build library | `bun run build` |
| Run tests | `bun run test` |
| Generate types | `bun run cf-typegen` |

## Gotchas

- **wrangler.jsonc** — DO bindings must match exports. Active DOs: `UserConnection`, `PresenceRoom`, `ChatRoom`. Remove any stale bindings (CounterActor, ChatExample, etc.) or wrangler dev will fail.
- **Test snapshots** — May be outdated; update with `bun run test -- --run --update`.
- **RoomDO binding** — Example `onConnect` may throw "RoomDO binding not found" at runtime; WebSocket handling works otherwise.
- **Docs site** (`site/`) — Separate workspace; run `cd site && bun run dev` independently.

## Folder Structure

- `src/` — Core library (actor/, client/, shared/, typed/)
- `examples/` — Example apps and server definitions
- `site/` — Documentation site (separate workspace)
